<title>LITHUANIA: LITHUANIA - C.BANK RESERVES UP TO $883.3 MLN IN MAY.</title>
<headline>LITHUANIA - C.BANK RESERVES UP TO $883.3 MLN IN MAY.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The central bank said on Friday that its official reserves rose to $883.3 million in May versus $842 million the month before.</p>
<p>It also said in a statement that convertible currency was $812.7 million in May compared to $770.3 million in April, gold reserves remained unchanged at $62.1 million and holdings of SDRs were down to $8.5 million in May from $9.6 in April.</p>
<p>-- Andrius Vilkancas, Vilnius newsromm +370 2 22 35 17</p>
